<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">San Remo conference</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1920">1920</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The San Remo conference was a meeting of the Allied Supreme Council held at Sanremo in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in April 1920. It assigned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations-mandate">League of Nations mandates</a> over former Ottoman territories, giving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lebanon">Lebanon</a>, and endorsed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balfour-declaration">Balfour Declaration</a>'s promise of a Jewish national home. Its decisions led to the French occupation of Syria and the creation of Mandatory Palestine and Mandatory <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/san-remo-conference.jpg" alt="San Remo conference" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:San_Remo_Conference_1920.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
